{"text": "In this town, everyone has a bunker. Except me, my name is Jake. Ten years ago, the zombie apocalypse began. Every family was given an underground bunker, but no two bunkers were the same. Bunker number one was made entirely of glass, deep beneath the ocean. Bunker number seven was a luxury mansion with a pool, movie theater, and unlimited food. Bunker number 12 had one rule, never make a sound. And bunker number 66 had one hundred metal doors, but nobody could open the last one. Some people lived like kings, but me. I slept inside an abandoned gas station, hiding from zombies every night. Until I noticed something strange, the zombies never attacked me. They chased everyone else, but whenever I walked past, they just stopped and stared. So one day, I followed them. They led me beneath an abandoned hospital to a giant metal door, bunker 100. When I touched it, it opened. Inside were hundreds of security monitors, showing every bunker in the city. And in the middle was a giant screen. It displayed every person's name, but when I searched for mine, nothing. Instead, a message appeared. Subject zero has returned. Suddenly, every screen turned red. All bunkers initiate lockdown. I turned around. Hundreds of zombies stood behind me, but they weren't attacking. They were waiting. Then, an old recording appeared. A scientist holding a newborn baby. That baby was me. And underneath were the words, the first infected. That's when I understood. The bunkers weren't built to protect people from zombies. They were built to protect everyone from me. And for the first time in 10 years, every zombie bowed down. But suddenly, another message appeared. Subject zero has been activated. A countdown began. 10, 9, 8, then every bunker door in the city started opening. And a voice whispered. Phase two has begun.", "words": [{"w": " In", "s": 0.0, "e": 0.22}, {"w": " this", "s": 0.22, "e": 0.44}, {"w": " town,", "s": 0.44, "e": 0.9}, {"w": " everyone", "s": 1.36, "e": 1.6}, {"w":